            <ArticleTitle>Chronic perineal pain and lower urinary tract dysfunction--a clinical feature of the &quot;Gulf War syndrome&quot;?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>213-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A Persian Gulf War veteran presented to the University Neuro-Urology service for management of severe chronic perineal pain. The overall physical and neurological exam was unremarkable. However, the rectal exam and the urodynamic study revealed a severe pelvic floor dysfunction. A neuro-behavioral approach is recommended and discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
